        ...,
        description="Path to input H5 file",
        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-f", "--hdf5")},
    )", "explanation": "Passing arbitrary keyword arguments such as `cli=` to `Field` is deprecated in Pydantic V2 (the source of the collection failure). Move them into `json_schema_extra`, which V2 documents as the replacement, keeping the same key and value."}, {"finding_ids": ["pydantic_cli/examples/simple_with_boolean_custom.py:5:moved-import"], "search": "        cli=("-b", "--beta-filter"),", "replace": "        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-b", "--beta-filter")},", "explanation": "Same deprecated extra kwarg `cli=` on `Field` (Pydantic V2.0 deprecation). Moved into `json_schema_extra` with the same value. This line was not in the reported failure list but fails identically on import."}, {"finding_ids": ["pydantic_cli/examples/simple_with_boolean_custom.py:5:moved-import"], "search": "        cli=("--epsilon", "--disable-epsilon"),", "replace": "        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("--epsilon", "--disable-epsilon")},", "explanation": "Same deprecated extra kwarg `cli=` on `Field`. Moved into `json_schema_extra` per the V2 migration guide, value unchanged."}], "notes": "Edits are needed for the remaining v1 APIs in this file. (1) The `from pydantic.fields import Field` import is replaced with a top-level `from pydantic import ... Field`. (2) All three `cli=` extra kwargs on `Field` (input_file3, beta_filter, epsilon) are moved into `json_schema_extra={"cli": ...}`. The reported failure only named input_file3, but the other two fail the same way. Config: the `class Config(DefaultConfig)` finding (line 20) is already migrated to `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` in the current content, so it is left alone. Optional-no-default findings (lines 38 and 55): `outfile: Optional[str] = None` and `gamma: Optional[bool] = None` already have explicit `= None` defaults, so no change is needed. Dependency caveat: pydantic_cli/core.py (also in the migration set) must read the CLI flag tuple from `field.json_schema_extra["cli"]` rather than the removed `field.extra`. If core.py still reads `field.extra`, this file will import cleanly but the custom flags will not be applied. That change belongs in core.py, not here."}
